## Phase 5 — tc Shaping Inside Pods

### Per-Slice QoS Profile

| Slice | tc Type | Rate | Ceil | Latency (netem) | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **eMBB** | HTB | 100mbit | 100mbit | — | High throughput streaming |
| **URLLC** | HTB + netem | 50mbit | 50mbit | 1ms | Ultra-low latency |
| **mMTC** | HTB | 1mbit | 5mbit | — | Low bandwidth IoT |

### Runtime Verification

```bash
# Exec into a UPF pod and inspect tc
kubectl exec -n embb deploy/upf-embb -- tc qdisc show dev ogstun-embb
kubectl exec -n urllc deploy/upf-urllc -- tc qdisc show dev ogstun-urllc
kubectl exec -n mmtc deploy/upf-mmtc -- tc qdisc show dev ogstun-mmtc
```

---

## Phase 6 — Namespace-Based Service Isolation

Even though UPF traffic uses `hostNetwork`, the **namespace separation gives you**:

| Benefit | How |
|---|---|
| **Logical isolation** | Each UPF is in its own namespace (`embb`, `urllc`, `mmtc`) |
| **RBAC policies** | Restrict who can `exec` into URLLC vs mMTC pods |
| **NetworkPolicies** | Future: add Calico/Cilium CNI for pod-level firewall rules |
| **Resource Quotas** | Limit CPU/memory per namespace per slice |
| **Monitoring** | Slice-specific metrics via namespace labels |
| **Independent scaling** | Scale eMBB UPF independently of URLLC |

### Example: Resource Quota per Slice

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ResourceQuota
metadata:
  name: upf-quota
  namespace: urllc
spec:
  hard:
    requests.cpu: "1"
    requests.memory: 512Mi
    limits.cpu: "2"
    limits.memory: 1Gi
```

---

## Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| `hostNetwork` pods conflict on ports | UPF won't start | Only one UPF per PFCP/GTP-U port; stop native UPFs first |
| Minikube single-node limits | Resource contention | Use resource limits + monitor with `kubectl top` |
| `privileged: true` security | Container escape risk | Acceptable for research; production would use SELinux + specific caps |
| Kubernetes restarts UPF pod | PFCP association breaks | SMF heartbeat will re-establish; add `restartPolicy: Always` |
| GTP-U IP `192.168.49.144/146` not bound to `ens33` | URLLC/mMTC GTP-U unreachable | Must add secondary IPs to `ens33` as before |
| Docker image pulls Open5GS version mismatch | Config incompatibility | Pin version `open5gs=2.7.6~jammy` in Dockerfile |

